const e="aiu-inter-university-youth-festival",d=2026,t="Read in full: the 21-page AIU Rules and Regulations (page 1 is the Events at a Glance table, a one-page copy of which was also read). Not printed in the source: festival dates, venue and host university, a registration deadline, how or where entries are submitted (no online form is described), prizes, certificates and trophy names other than the Overall Championship Trophy and category trophies, and marks per judging factor. The source prints no contact phone number; only the email address. Differences kept as printed: the general guidelines say the contingent leader deposits one university flag with the host and keeps one for the procession, while the Cultural Procession rule says Team Managers deposit two flags at the desk near the registration desk. The events at a glance table prints a minimum time of 120 minutes for the Fine Arts events, while the rules print a total of 2 hours 30 minutes. Hindi Elocution (Vagmita) and Hindi Debate (Vaad Vivaad) are separate events in the source and are written into the Elocution and Debate rows. The template's Students Solo and Students Team age groups (17 to 24) are a working band: the source gives only 'less than 25 on 1 July' with no minimum age, so no age group row is written and the age rule sits in Page eligibility.",n={Title:"Rules & Criteria",Subtitle:"AIU 39th Inter-University Youth Festival (UNIFESTs) 2025-26. Read these rules before you register.",NoticeTitle:"Please Read Before Registering",Notice:"Each university may send only one entry in each event. Only full-time students under 25 years of age on {{AgeLimitDate}} can take part. The registration fee is {{RegistrationFee}}.",Notes:["Questions about the festival: {{QueriesContact}}."],Sections:[{Key:"general",Title:"General Rules",Items:["These rules and regulations are for the Association of Indian Universities (AIU) Inter-University Youth Festival (UNIFESTs), 39th edition, 2025-26. They apply to both the zonal festivals and the national festival.","The programme has 28 events: Music (9), Dance (3), Literary (5), Theatre (4), Fine Arts (6) and the Cultural Procession.","The performance time of every event is the same at the zonal and the national festival.","To promote creativity, cultural contingents are requested to present new cultural items as far as possible in all competitions of the festival.","The events at a glance table prints, for each event, the most participants, the most accompanists, the most people in total, and the least and most time in minutes. Each competition's own rules repeat these limits."]},{Key:"eligibility",Title:"Eligibility",Items:["Only bonafide, full-time students can take part. The student must be enrolled in a degree, postgraduate degree or diploma course of at least one academic year, and the examination must be conducted by the university or by a college affiliated to a university, after passing the 12th class examination.","Students of open universities are bonafide students and can take part if they meet the other conditions.","Only students who are less than 25 years of age on {{AgeLimitDate}} can take part. There is no minimum age.","A student cannot represent more than one university in one academic year.","Provisional admission to a course at a university or college does not make a student eligible to represent that university.","A student who is employed full-time is not eligible.","A student who migrates from one university to another is eligible only after the admission in the new university is regularized and the new university admits the student as a bonafide student.","Universities and institutions must pay the AIU subscription fee to take part in AIU Youth Affairs programmes.","Participants must carry identity cards with a photograph, signed by the proper authority of their university.","If a participant is found to be ineligible, that participant is disqualified. The university is then automatically disqualified from every event in which that student took part."]},{Key:"registration",Title:"How to Register",Items:["Each participant, including each team official, deposits the registration fee: {{RegistrationFee}}.","Each university deposits the refundable caution money at the host university's registration desk or venue, or through digital mode in advance: {{CautionMoney}}.","Send two stamp-size photographs of each participant, each accompanist and each official delegate to the host university in advance.","The contingent leader deposits one university flag with the host university and keeps one university flag for the Cultural Procession.","Some events need printed notes or a synopsis at registration. See the rules of Folk / Tribal Dance, Classical Dance, Creative Choreography, One Act Play and Skit."]},{Key:"fees",Title:"Fees and Payment",Items:["Registration fee: {{RegistrationFee}}.","Caution money (refundable): {{CautionMoney}}.","The participating university pays its own travelling expenses."]},{Key:"teams",Title:"Entries and Contingent",Items:["Each university may send only one entry in each event.","A contingent has at most 60 members. The 60 include 1 Dean or Director (or an equivalent representative), 2 Team Managers (preferably one male and one female), the student participants, the student accompanists and the professional accompanists.","A university that has female participants is advised to send one female Team Manager as a must.","A university may bring as many student and professional accompanists as its performances need, if the total contingent does not go above 60.","Two universities may share professional accompanists. The accompanist then counts in both contingents and the fees are charged to both universities."]},{Key:"levels",Title:"Zonal and National Festivals",Items:["The festival is held at zonal level and at national level. The same rules and performance times apply at both.","At the national festival, at most 2 members of a university's zonal contingent may be replaced, in unforeseen circumstances. A replaced member is not eligible to take part in any solo event."]},{Key:"points",Title:"Points",Items:["Points for the overall trophy and the category trophies are given for First, Second and Third place. The points are different for group events and solo events.","The Cultural Procession is an additional event. Its marks, with the marks of the other events, count toward the Overall Championship Trophy."]},{Key:"conduct",Title:"Conduct and Safety",Items:["If the behaviour of any contingent is against the objectives of the festival, the host university may take suitable action against the members concerned. An individual or a team may be debarred from taking part in future youth festivals for three years, and AIU is told.","No official or member of any university may make press statements on controversial issues.","Drinking liquor or being intoxicated, eve-teasing, influencing adjudicators and indecent behaviour inside the campus and the venue are strictly prohibited. The AIU Cultural Committee decides the disciplinary action. It can include debarring the university team or official from inter-university youth activities for a period it decides.","Participants are strongly advised not to use materials or props that involve fire, inflammable substances, direct fuel, fireworks, arms, weapons or any other item that can be dangerous to people or to the host university's buildings.","If such materials are needed for cultural or artistic expression, get prior written approval from the host university well in advance. The host university can refuse any such material that it thinks is unsafe or harmful to its premises or to the audience.","This advice is given for safety and smooth running. It does not remove the safety duties of participants or organizers.","Competitors take part entirely at their own risk. Neither the host nor AIU is responsible for any unfortunate event.","Students should dress appropriately, keeping in mind the weather and the cultural spirit of the youth festival."]},{Key:"judging",Title:"Judging and Time Limits",Items:["The decision of the jury members appointed for each event is final and binding on all. It is expected that the judgment is respected.","Seven events are marked with a star in the events at a glance table: Light Vocal (Indian), Western Vocal (Solo), Vagmita (Hindi Elocution), Elocution (English), Debate (English), Vaad Vivaad (Hindi Debate) and Mimicry. These get a grace time of 15 seconds.","All other events get a grace time of 30 seconds."]},{Key:"complaints",Title:"Protests and Appeals",Items:["If a team is not satisfied with a judgment, the matter may be referred to the Jury of Appeals.","Lodge a protest with the Organizing Secretary or Convener of the competition within one hour of the end of the competition.","No protest is accepted on matters of judgment.","A protest is accepted on a violation of rules or improper conduct of the contest. The protest fee is {{ProtestFee}}. It is not refunded unless the Jury of Appeals upholds the protest.","No appeal can be made against the decision of the Jury of Appeals."]},{Key:"other",Title:"Food, Lodging and What to Bring",Items:["The host university provides meals from lunch one day before the festival begins until breakfast on the morning after the valedictory ceremony.","Free board and lodging is provided to the participating teams during the Inter Zonal and National Youth Festivals.","Participating university troupes may be lodged as guests in student hostels, using common rooms, verandas and similar spaces.","Lodging is from the night one day before the festival starts until the morning after the valedictory ceremony.","All participants and officials are advised to bring enough warm bedding, blankets, woollen clothing, essential medicines and locks for personal safety and comfort.","All members of the contingent are strongly advised to get vaccinated against cholera and typhoid before the journey."]}],Documents:[{Title:"AIU 39th Inter-University Youth Festival 2025-26: Rules and Regulations",Url:"https://mdsuajmer.ac.in/notifications/2190_Rules%20and%20Guidelines%20by%20AIU%20for%20youth%20fest.pdf"},{Title:"AIU 39th Inter-University Youth Festival 2025-26: Events at a Glance",Url:"https://aiu.ac.in/wp-content/uploads/docs/2025/12/Final_Events_at_a_Glance.pdf"}]},a=[{ParticipantType:"Individual",Source:"Events at a Glance note b (point system)",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:["Solo events: First place 5 points, Second place 3 points, Third place 1 point (5-3-1)."],Notes:null},Markdown:`## Points
- Solo events: First place 5 points, Second place 3 points, Third place 1 point (5-3-1).`},{ParticipantType:"Team",Source:"Events at a Glance note b (point system)",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:["Group events: First place 9 points, Second place 7 points, Third place 5 points (9-7-5)."],Notes:null},Markdown:`## Points
- Group events: First place 9 points, Second place 7 points, Third place 5 points (9-7-5).`}],i=[],s=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Classical Vocal Solo","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.2-6 (Music)","Sections":{"About":["Hindustani or Karnatak (Carnatic) classical vocal solo. The item can be presented in either style."],"TimeAndFormat":["The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.","The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes."],"Rules":["One participant. At most 3 accompanists are permitted.","Accompaniment must be live. Recorded music is not permitted.","Sufficient thought and care must be used in the choice of Raga and composition."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Cinema songs are not allowed in this item."],"Judging":["Judgment is based on qualities such as Taal, selection of Raga, elaboration of Raga, composition, Alap, Taan, Layakari and overall impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Hindustani or Karnatak (Carnatic) classical vocal solo. The item can be presented in either style.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.\\n- The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One participant. At most 3 accompanists are permitted.\\n- Accompaniment must be live. Recorded music is not permitted.\\n- Sufficient thought and care must be used in the choice of Raga and composition.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Cinema songs are not allowed in this item.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is based on qualities such as Taal, selection of Raga, elaboration of Raga, composition, Alap, Taan, Layakari and overall impression."},{"Title":"Classical Instrumental Solo (Percussion)","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.2-6 (Music)","Sections":{"About":["Percussion (Tal Vadya) classical instrumental solo. The item can be presented in either the Hindustani or the Carnatic style."],"TimeAndFormat":["The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.","The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes."],"Rules":["One participant. At most 3 accompanists are permitted.","Accompaniment must be live. Recorded music is not permitted.","Participants must bring their own instruments."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgment is based on qualities such as Taal, selection of Raga, composition, Kayada, Rela, Tukda, Layakari and overall impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Percussion (Tal Vadya) classical instrumental solo. The item can be presented in either the Hindustani or the Carnatic style.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.\\n- The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One participant. At most 3 accompanists are permitted.\\n- Accompaniment must be live. Recorded music is not permitted.\\n- Participants must bring their own instruments.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is based on qualities such as Taal, selection of Raga, composition, Kayada, Rela, Tukda, Layakari and overall impression."},{"Title":"Classical Instrumental Solo (Non-Percussion)","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.2-6 (Music)","Sections":{"About":["Non-percussion (Swar Vadya) classical instrumental solo. The item can be presented in either the Hindustani or the Carnatic style."],"TimeAndFormat":["The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.","The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes."],"Rules":["One participant. At most 3 accompanists are permitted.","Accompaniment must be live. Recorded music is not permitted.","Participants must bring their own instruments."],"Allowed":["Instruments of Western origin that have been adopted into the Indian Raga system are allowed."],"NotAllowed":["Casio is not allowed."],"Judging":["Judgment is based on qualities such as Swara, Taal, selection of Raga, elaboration of Raga, Alap, Taan, Layakari, composition and overall impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Non-percussion (Swar Vadya) classical instrumental solo. The item can be presented in either the Hindustani or the Carnatic style.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.\\n- The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One participant. At most 3 accompanists are permitted.\\n- Accompaniment must be live. Recorded music is not permitted.\\n- Participants must bring their own instruments.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Instruments of Western origin that have been adopted into the Indian Raga system are allowed.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Casio is not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is based on qualities such as Swara, Taal, selection of Raga, elaboration of Raga, Alap, Taan, Layakari, composition and overall impression."},{"Title":"Light Vocal (Indian)","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.2-6 (Music)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The performance lasts between 4 and 6 minutes.","The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 3 minutes."],"Rules":["One participant. At most 3 accompanists are permitted.","Accompaniment must be live. Recorded music is not permitted."],"Allowed":["Only non-film songs such as Geet, Ghazal, Bhajan, Shabad and Abhangas may be presented."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgment is based on qualities such as Swara, Taal, selection of Raga, selection of song, aesthetics, pronunciation, expression, composition and overall impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The performance lasts between 4 and 6 minutes.\\n- The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One participant. At most 3 accompanists are permitted.\\n- Accompaniment must be live. Recorded music is not permitted.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Only non-film songs such as Geet, Ghazal, Bhajan, Shabad and Abhangas may be presented.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is based on qualities such as Swara, Taal, selection of Raga, selection of song, aesthetics, pronunciation, expression, composition and overall impression."},{"Title":"Western Vocal Solo","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.2-6 (Music)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The performance lasts between 4 and 6 minutes.","The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 3 minutes."],"Rules":["One participant. At most 3 accompanists are permitted.","The language of the song must be English.","Accompaniment must be live."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Recorded music, musical patches and keyboard presets are not allowed."],"Judging":["Judgment is based on qualities such as composition, rhythm, coordination and overall impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The performance lasts between 4 and 6 minutes.\\n- The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One participant. At most 3 accompanists are permitted.\\n- The language of the song must be English.\\n- Accompaniment must be live.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Recorded music, musical patches and keyboard presets are not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is based on qualities such as composition, rhythm, coordination and overall impression."},{"Title":"Group Song (Indian)","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.2-6 (Music)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.","The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes."],"Rules":["A group may have up to six singers.","At most 5 accompanists are permitted.","Each team must present two songs: one patriotic song and one folk song.","The group songs should be chosen from Indian music and may be in any regional language.","Accompaniment must be live. Recorded music, musical patches and keyboard presets are not allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Film songs are not permitted as group songs."],"Judging":["Judgment is based only on the quality of singing, selection of song, pronunciation, theka and coordination. It is not based on makeup, costumes or stage actions."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.\\n- The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A group may have up to six singers.\\n- At most 5 accompanists are permitted.\\n- Each team must present two songs: one patriotic song and one folk song.\\n- The group songs should be chosen from Indian music and may be in any regional language.\\n- Accompaniment must be live. Recorded music, musical patches and keyboard presets are not allowed.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Film songs are not permitted as group songs.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is based only on the quality of singing, selection of song, pronunciation, theka and coordination. It is not based on makeup, costumes or stage actions."},{"Title":"Group Song (Western)","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.2-6 (Music)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.","The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes."],"Rules":["A group may have at most six singers.","At most 5 accompanists are permitted.","The group songs must be in the English language.","Accompaniment must be live. Recorded music, musical patches and keyboard presets are not allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgment is based only on the quality of singing. It is not based on makeup, costumes or stage actions of the team."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.\\n- The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A group may have at most six singers.\\n- At most 5 accompanists are permitted.\\n- The group songs must be in the English language.\\n- Accompaniment must be live. Recorded music, musical patches and keyboard presets are not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is based only on the quality of singing. It is not based on makeup, costumes or stage actions of the team."},{"Title":"Folk Orchestra","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.2-6 (Music)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.","The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 10 minutes."],"Rules":["The team has at most 12 performers: not more than 9 participants and 3 accompanists.","At most three accompanists are permitted. They must wear attire different from the student participants so that they can be easily identified. They must sit or stand separately from the participants and must not lead the team. The judges make sure of this through introductions and other means.","Accompaniment must be live. Recorded music is not permitted.","The team should preferably present folk tunes that are recognized as belonging to the state of the university.","The instruments used should mainly be those traditionally linked with folk music."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Singing is strictly prohibited.","Dance during a folk orchestra performance is discouraged."],"Judging":["Marking is based only on the quality of the music composed.","Efforts to improve visual appeal through set design, orchestration and similar means are not considered in evaluation or marking."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.\\n- The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The team has at most 12 performers: not more than 9 participants and 3 accompanists.\\n- At most three accompanists are permitted. They must wear attire different from the student participants so that they can be easily identified. They must sit or stand separately from the participants and must not lead the team. The judges make sure of this through introductions and other means.\\n- Accompaniment must be live. Recorded music is not permitted.\\n- The team should preferably present folk tunes that are recognized as belonging to the state of the university.\\n- The instruments used should mainly be those traditionally linked with folk music.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Singing is strictly prohibited.\\n- Dance during a folk orchestra performance is discouraged.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Marking is based only on the quality of the music composed.\\n- Efforts to improve visual appeal through set design, orchestration and similar means are not considered in evaluation or marking."},{"Title":"Western Instrumental Solo","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.2-6 (Music)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The performance lasts between 6 and 8 minutes.","The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes."],"Rules":["One participant. At most 3 accompanists are permitted.","Each participant performs Western music on any percussion or non-percussion instrument.","The participant may perform in any one genre or style, or mix several genres or styles of Western music.","Accompaniment must be live."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Recorded music, musical patches and keyboard presets are not allowed."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The performance lasts between 6 and 8 minutes.\\n- The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One participant. At most 3 accompanists are permitted.\\n- Each participant performs Western music on any percussion or non-percussion instrument.\\n- The participant may perform in any one genre or style, or mix several genres or styles of Western music.\\n- Accompaniment must be live.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Recorded music, musical patches and keyboard presets are not allowed."},{"Title":"Folk / Tribal Dance","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.6-8 (Dance)","Sections":{"About":["The dance may be a primitive or folk dance (Indian style) or a tribal dance of India."],"TimeAndFormat":["The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.","The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 10 minutes."],"Rules":["A team has at most 10 participants.","At most 5 accompanists are permitted.","Submit three copies of a brief note on the theme (Hindi or English), and the text of the song if there is one, with the entry form at registration.","The team removes its sets and properties itself, immediately after the performance."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["A classical dance is not allowed in this item.","Recorded music and audio or CDs are not permitted. Accompaniment must be live."],"Judging":["Judgment is based on rhythm, formation, expression, costumes, make-up, sets and overall effect.","Marking is strictly based on the quality of dance. Extra effort to improve visual appeal through set design is not considered."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The dance may be a primitive or folk dance (Indian style) or a tribal dance of India.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.\\n- The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A team has at most 10 participants.\\n- At most 5 accompanists are permitted.\\n- Submit three copies of a brief note on the theme (Hindi or English), and the text of the song if there is one, with the entry form at registration.\\n- The team removes its sets and properties itself, immediately after the performance.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- A classical dance is not allowed in this item.\\n- Recorded music and audio or CDs are not permitted. Accompaniment must be live.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is based on rhythm, formation, expression, costumes, make-up, sets and overall effect.\\n- Marking is strictly based on the quality of dance. Extra effort to improve visual appeal through set design is not considered."},{"Title":"Classical Dance","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.6-8 (Dance)","Sections":{"About":["The classical dance can be from any approved school of dance: Kathak, Kathakali, Bharatnatyam, Manipuri, Kuchipudi, Mohiniyattam, Odissi or Sattriya."],"TimeAndFormat":["The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.","The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes."],"Rules":["One participant. At most 5 accompanists are permitted.","Submit three copies of a brief note on the dance story, if any, and on the accompanying song with its meaning in Hindi or English, at registration."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Recorded music and audio or CDs are not permitted. Accompaniment must be live."],"Judging":["Judgment is based on qualities such as Taal, technique, rhythm, Abhinaya (expression), costumes, footwork and overall impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The classical dance can be from any approved school of dance: Kathak, Kathakali, Bharatnatyam, Manipuri, Kuchipudi, Mohiniyattam, Odissi or Sattriya.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.\\n- The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One participant. At most 5 accompanists are permitted.\\n- Submit three copies of a brief note on the dance story, if any, and on the accompanying song with its meaning in Hindi or English, at registration.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Recorded music and audio or CDs are not permitted. Accompaniment must be live.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is based on qualities such as Taal, technique, rhythm, Abhinaya (expression), costumes, footwork and overall impression."},{"Title":"Creative Choreography","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.6-8 (Dance)","Sections":{"About":["The performance must show a clear theme or message through dance, using a single dance form or style or a fusion of several. The theme should be suitable for public viewing and preferably youth-centric, nation-centric or about social issues."],"TimeAndFormat":["The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.","The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes."],"Rules":["A team has at most 12 participants.","At most three accompanists are permitted. They may help with props, technical cues, background narration or effects. They should stay off stage and may be seen for a moment while doing these duties. They are not part of the performance. Their role is only to support.","Submit three copies of a brief note on the theme with the entry form at registration.","Teams must bring or arrange their own props, if any."],"Allowed":["Recorded music is allowed. Teams should take care when choosing songs so that the essence and spirit of the Youth Festival are kept."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Choreography is judged on theme and message clarity, choreography and creativity, synchronization and coordination, use of stage and props, costumes, and overall impact.","Extra effort to improve visual appeal through set design is not considered for marking."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The performance must show a clear theme or message through dance, using a single dance form or style or a fusion of several. The theme should be suitable for public viewing and preferably youth-centric, nation-centric or about social issues.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.\\n- The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A team has at most 12 participants.\\n- At most three accompanists are permitted. They may help with props, technical cues, background narration or effects. They should stay off stage and may be seen for a moment while doing these duties. They are not part of the performance. Their role is only to support.\\n- Submit three copies of a brief note on the theme with the entry form at registration.\\n- Teams must bring or arrange their own props, if any.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Recorded music is allowed. Teams should take care when choosing songs so that the essence and spirit of the Youth Festival are kept.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Choreography is judged on theme and message clarity, choreography and creativity, synchronization and coordination, use of stage and props, costumes, and overall impact.\\n- Extra effort to improve visual appeal through set design is not considered for marking."},{"Title":"General Quiz","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.8 (Literary - General Quiz)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["There is a written preliminary round, and teams are chosen for the final.","The final is oral and includes audio-visual questions."],"Rules":["A team has 3 participants.","The evaluation procedure, the time allowed to answer each question and the types of rounds are announced before the competition starts."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The Quiz Master's decisions are final and binding in all matters, including question types, rounds, marking scheme and tie-breaking."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- There is a written preliminary round, and teams are chosen for the final.\\n- The final is oral and includes audio-visual questions.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A team has 3 participants.\\n- The evaluation procedure, the time allowed to answer each question and the types of rounds are announced before the competition starts.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The Quiz Master's decisions are final and binding in all matters, including question types, rounds, marking scheme and tie-breaking."},{"Title":"Elocution","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.8-9 (Literary - Elocution English and Hindi)","Sections":{"About":["Elocution is held in two languages: English, and Hindi (Vagmita, वाग्मिता). Each is a separate event in the programme."],"TimeAndFormat":["Each speaker speaks for between 4 and 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Each university is represented by one speaker in each language.","The medium of expression is English only in the English event and Hindi only in the Hindi event.","The subject or topic is announced at the managers' meeting.","The performance is judged in one language.","The item is prose or poetry, and not a song."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Reading from paper or any other source is strictly prohibited."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Elocution is held in two languages: English, and Hindi (Vagmita, वाग्मिता). Each is a separate event in the programme.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Each speaker speaks for between 4 and 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each university is represented by one speaker in each language.\\n- The medium of expression is English only in the English event and Hindi only in the Hindi event.\\n- The subject or topic is announced at the managers' meeting.\\n- The performance is judged in one language.\\n- The item is prose or poetry, and not a song.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Reading from paper or any other source is strictly prohibited."},{"Title":"Debate","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.9 (Literary - Debate English and Hindi)","Sections":{"About":["Debate is held in two languages: English, and Hindi (Vaad Vivaad, वाद-विवाद). Each is a separate event in the programme."],"TimeAndFormat":["Each debater speaks for between 4 and 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Each university is represented by two debaters in each language: one speaks FOR the motion and the other speaks AGAINST it.","The medium of expression is English only in the English event and Hindi only in the Hindi event.","The subject or topic is announced at the managers' meeting."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Reading from paper or any other source is strictly prohibited."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Debate is held in two languages: English, and Hindi (Vaad Vivaad, वाद-विवाद). Each is a separate event in the programme.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Each debater speaks for between 4 and 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each university is represented by two debaters in each language: one speaks FOR the motion and the other speaks AGAINST it.\\n- The medium of expression is English only in the English event and Hindi only in the Hindi event.\\n- The subject or topic is announced at the managers' meeting.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Reading from paper or any other source is strictly prohibited."},{"Title":"One Act Play","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.10 (Theatre - One Act Play)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The performance lasts between 25 and 30 minutes.","Timing begins as soon as the signal is given or the team starts the introduction, whichever is earlier.","Up to 15 minutes are allowed for setting the stage and for removing sets and properties after the team takes charge of the stage. The team must clear the stage strictly after the performance."],"Rules":["The number of participants must not be more than nine.","At most 5 accompanists are permitted.","Accompanists speak from the background or play musical instruments for background music. They do not appear on the stage.","The team brings its own sets, stage properties, makeup materials and so on. Light and general properties such as ordinary furniture may be provided on prior request.","Participants may speak in Hindi, English or any regional language of India. If a regional language is used, submit a synopsis of the play with a translation in English or Hindi to the competition in-charge on the day of registration."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgment is mainly based on the qualities of the play, such as theme, acting, stagecraft, design and overall impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The performance lasts between 25 and 30 minutes.\\n- Timing begins as soon as the signal is given or the team starts the introduction, whichever is earlier.\\n- Up to 15 minutes are allowed for setting the stage and for removing sets and properties after the team takes charge of the stage. The team must clear the stage strictly after the performance.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The number of participants must not be more than nine.\\n- At most 5 accompanists are permitted.\\n- Accompanists speak from the background or play musical instruments for background music. They do not appear on the stage.\\n- The team brings its own sets, stage properties, makeup materials and so on. Light and general properties such as ordinary furniture may be provided on prior request.\\n- Participants may speak in Hindi, English or any regional language of India. If a regional language is used, submit a synopsis of the play with a translation in English or Hindi to the competition in-charge on the day of registration.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is mainly based on the qualities of the play, such as theme, acting, stagecraft, design and overall impression."},{"Title":"Skit","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.10-11 (Theatre - Skit)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.","The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes."],"Rules":["At most six participants are allowed.","At most 3 accompanists are permitted.","Submit three copies of the synopsis of the skit's theme, with the language of presentation (Hindi or English), on the day of registration.","Only innocent satire or humour is expected."],"Allowed":["Makeup, drapery and background music are allowed."],"NotAllowed":["Personal remarks, aspersions and character assassination are not permitted.","Vulgarity and bitter insinuations must be strictly avoided."],"Judging":["The item is judged mainly on qualities such as theme, acting, stagecraft, design and overall impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The performance lasts between 8 and 10 minutes.\\n- The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At most six participants are allowed.\\n- At most 3 accompanists are permitted.\\n- Submit three copies of the synopsis of the skit's theme, with the language of presentation (Hindi or English), on the day of registration.\\n- Only innocent satire or humour is expected.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Makeup, drapery and background music are allowed.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Personal remarks, aspersions and character assassination are not permitted.\\n- Vulgarity and bitter insinuations must be strictly avoided.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The item is judged mainly on qualities such as theme, acting, stagecraft, design and overall impression."},{"Title":"Mime","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.11 (Theatre - Mime)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The performance lasts between 4 and 5 minutes.","The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 1 minutes."],"Rules":["At most six participants are allowed.","At most 2 accompanists are permitted."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgment is mainly based on qualities such as idea, creativity of presentation, use of makeup, music and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The performance lasts between 4 and 5 minutes.\\n- The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 1 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At most six participants are allowed.\\n- At most 2 accompanists are permitted.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment is mainly based on qualities such as idea, creativity of presentation, use of makeup, music and general impression."},{"Title":"Mimicry","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.11 (Theatre - Mimicry)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The performance lasts between 4 and 5 minutes.","The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 2 minutes."],"Rules":["One participant."],"Allowed":["Participants may mimic sounds of machines and speeches of well-known persons, including film personalities."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Marking is based on skill of imitation, variety of sounds and voices imitated, and overall presentation."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The performance lasts between 4 and 5 minutes.\\n- The time for stage setup, instrument arrangement, sound check and overall readiness is at most 2 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One participant.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Participants may mimic sounds of machines and speeches of well-known persons, including film personalities.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Marking is based on skill of imitation, variety of sounds and voices imitated, and overall presentation."},{"Title":"On the Spot Painting","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.12 (Fine Arts - On the Spot Painting)","Sections":{"About":["The painting is made on the spot on a theme or subject announced at the start of the competition."],"TimeAndFormat":["Participants get a total of 2 hours and 30 minutes to finish the artwork. The events at a glance table prints a minimum of 120 minutes and a maximum of 150 minutes."],"Rules":["One participant.","The host institute provides half imperial size drawing paper (22 inch x 15 inch) and the work is made on it.","Participants use any one medium, such as acrylic colours, water colours, poster colours, pastel colours or oil colours.","Participants bring their own art supplies, including brushes, colours, palettes, containers and any other tools they need. Only the drawing sheet is provided.","Participants are advised to bring their own drawing boards or easel."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["The use or possession of mobile phones and other digital devices is strictly prohibited for participants throughout the event."],"Judging":["Paintings are evaluated on relevance to theme, creativity and originality, composition and layout, colour harmony and technique, and overall aesthetic appeal."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The painting is made on the spot on a theme or subject announced at the start of the competition.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Participants get a total of 2 hours and 30 minutes to finish the artwork. The events at a glance table prints a minimum of 120 minutes and a maximum of 150 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One participant.\\n- The host institute provides half imperial size drawing paper (22 inch x 15 inch) and the work is made on it.\\n- Participants use any one medium, such as acrylic colours, water colours, poster colours, pastel colours or oil colours.\\n- Participants bring their own art supplies, including brushes, colours, palettes, containers and any other tools they need. Only the drawing sheet is provided.\\n- Participants are advised to bring their own drawing boards or easel.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- The use or possession of mobile phones and other digital devices is strictly prohibited for participants throughout the event.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Paintings are evaluated on relevance to theme, creativity and originality, composition and layout, colour harmony and technique, and overall aesthetic appeal."},{"Title":"Collage","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.12-13 (Fine Arts - Collage)","Sections":{"About":["The collage is made on the spot on a theme or subject announced at the start of the competition."],"TimeAndFormat":["Participants get at most 2 hours and 30 minutes to finish the collage. The events at a glance table prints a minimum of 120 minutes and a maximum of 150 minutes."],"Rules":["One participant.","The host institute provides half imperial size drawing paper (22 inch x 15 inch) and the work is made on it.","Collages must be made only with materials from old magazines and newspapers.","Participants bring their own materials, including adhesive (pasting material), old magazines or newspapers and any other things they need.","All tearing and cutting must be done by hand."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Scissors, cutters, blades and any other sharp cutting tools are strictly prohibited.","The use or possession of mobile phones and other digital devices is strictly prohibited for participants throughout the event."],"Judging":["Collages are evaluated on relevance to theme, creativity and innovation, neatness and craftsmanship, composition and layout, and visual impact and aesthetic appeal."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The collage is made on the spot on a theme or subject announced at the start of the competition.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Participants get at most 2 hours and 30 minutes to finish the collage. The events at a glance table prints a minimum of 120 minutes and a maximum of 150 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One participant.\\n- The host institute provides half imperial size drawing paper (22 inch x 15 inch) and the work is made on it.\\n- Collages must be made only with materials from old magazines and newspapers.\\n- Participants bring their own materials, including adhesive (pasting material), old magazines or newspapers and any other things they need.\\n- All tearing and cutting must be done by hand.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Scissors, cutters, blades and any other sharp cutting tools are strictly prohibited.\\n- The use or possession of mobile phones and other digital devices is strictly prohibited for participants throughout the event.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Collages are evaluated on relevance to theme, creativity and innovation, neatness and craftsmanship, composition and layout, and visual impact and aesthetic appeal."},{"Title":"Poster Making","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.13 (Fine Arts - Poster Making)","Sections":{"About":["The poster is made on the spot on a theme or subject announced at the start of the competition."],"TimeAndFormat":["Participants get a total of 2 hours and 30 minutes to finish the artwork. The events at a glance table prints a minimum of 120 minutes and a maximum of 150 minutes."],"Rules":["One participant.","The host institute provides half imperial size drawing paper (22 inch x 15 inch) and the work is made on it.","Participants use any one medium, such as acrylic colours, water colours, poster colours or pastel colours.","Participants bring their own art supplies, including brushes, colours, palettes, containers and any other tools they need. Only the drawing sheet is provided.","Participants are advised to bring their own drawing boards or easel."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["The use or possession of mobile phones and other digital devices is strictly prohibited for participants throughout the event."],"Judging":["Posters are evaluated on relevance to the theme, creativity and originality, visual impact and presentation, clarity of message and visual communication, and overall composition and neatness."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The poster is made on the spot on a theme or subject announced at the start of the competition.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Participants get a total of 2 hours and 30 minutes to finish the artwork. The events at a glance table prints a minimum of 120 minutes and a maximum of 150 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One participant.\\n- The host institute provides half imperial size drawing paper (22 inch x 15 inch) and the work is made on it.\\n- Participants use any one medium, such as acrylic colours, water colours, poster colours or pastel colours.\\n- Participants bring their own art supplies, including brushes, colours, palettes, containers and any other tools they need. Only the drawing sheet is provided.\\n- Participants are advised to bring their own drawing boards or easel.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- The use or possession of mobile phones and other digital devices is strictly prohibited for participants throughout the event.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Posters are evaluated on relevance to the theme, creativity and originality, visual impact and presentation, clarity of message and visual communication, and overall composition and neatness."},{"Title":"Clay Modelling","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.14 (Fine Arts - Clay Modelling)","Sections":{"About":["The clay model is made on the spot on a theme or subject announced at the start of the competition."],"TimeAndFormat":["Participants get a total of 2 hours and 30 minutes to finish the artwork. The events at a glance table prints a minimum of 120 minutes and a maximum of 150 minutes."],"Rules":["One participant.","The largest size of the clay model is 12 inches x 12 inches x 12 inches (30 cm x 30 cm x 30 cm).","Participants must bring a wooden plank or plywood sheet of at least 2 feet x 2 feet and at least 12 millimetre thick, to use as the base of the clay model."],"Allowed":["Participants may bring clay modelling tools (shaping tools, rolling pins and modelling knives, all non-electric and hand-held), water sprays or small bowls for softening clay, cloths or rags for cleaning, and protective aprons or gloves.","Participants may use armatures and the tools needed to erect them."],"NotAllowed":["Electric or battery-operated tools, heating equipment, hair dryers and any powered tools are strictly prohibited.","Pre-molded or pre-designed parts are strictly prohibited.","External decorations are strictly prohibited. Paint, glitter, sequins, fabric and any other embellishments are not allowed.","Clay types other than the clay provided are strictly prohibited.","The use or possession of mobile phones and other digital devices is strictly prohibited for participants throughout the event."],"Judging":["Clay models are evaluated on relevance to the theme, creativity and originality, technique and detailing, structural stability, and aesthetic appeal and finish."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The clay model is made on the spot on a theme or subject announced at the start of the competition.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Participants get a total of 2 hours and 30 minutes to finish the artwork. The events at a glance table prints a minimum of 120 minutes and a maximum of 150 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One participant.\\n- The largest size of the clay model is 12 inches x 12 inches x 12 inches (30 cm x 30 cm x 30 cm).\\n- Participants must bring a wooden plank or plywood sheet of at least 2 feet x 2 feet and at least 12 millimetre thick, to use as the base of the clay model.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Participants may bring clay modelling tools (shaping tools, rolling pins and modelling knives, all non-electric and hand-held), water sprays or small bowls for softening clay, cloths or rags for cleaning, and protective aprons or gloves.\\n- Participants may use armatures and the tools needed to erect them.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Electric or battery-operated tools, heating equipment, hair dryers and any powered tools are strictly prohibited.\\n- Pre-molded or pre-designed parts are strictly prohibited.\\n- External decorations are strictly prohibited. Paint, glitter, sequins, fabric and any other embellishments are not allowed.\\n- Clay types other than the clay provided are strictly prohibited.\\n- The use or possession of mobile phones and other digital devices is strictly prohibited for participants throughout the event.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Clay models are evaluated on relevance to the theme, creativity and originality, technique and detailing, structural stability, and aesthetic appeal and finish."},{"Title":"Cartooning","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.14-15 (Fine Arts - Cartooning)","Sections":{"About":["The cartoon is made on the spot on a theme or subject announced at the start of the competition."],"TimeAndFormat":["Participants get a total of 2 hours and 30 minutes to finish the artwork. The events at a glance table prints a minimum of 120 minutes and a maximum of 150 minutes."],"Rules":["One participant.","The host institute provides half imperial size drawing paper (22 inch x 15 inch) and the work is made on it.","Participants use any one medium, such as acrylic colours, water colours, poster colours or pastel colours.","Participants bring their own art supplies, including brushes, colours, palettes, containers and any other tools they need. Only the drawing sheet is provided.","Participants are advised to bring their own drawing boards or easel."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["The use or possession of mobile phones and other digital devices is strictly prohibited for participants throughout the event."],"Judging":["Cartoons are evaluated on relevance to theme, creativity and originality, artistic composition and design, technique and use of medium, and overall visual impact."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The cartoon is made on the spot on a theme or subject announced at the start of the competition.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Participants get a total of 2 hours and 30 minutes to finish the artwork. The events at a glance table prints a minimum of 120 minutes and a maximum of 150 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One participant.\\n- The host institute provides half imperial size drawing paper (22 inch x 15 inch) and the work is made on it.\\n- Participants use any one medium, such as acrylic colours, water colours, poster colours or pastel colours.\\n- Participants bring their own art supplies, including brushes, colours, palettes, containers and any other tools they need. Only the drawing sheet is provided.\\n- Participants are advised to bring their own drawing boards or easel.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- The use or possession of mobile phones and other digital devices is strictly prohibited for participants throughout the event.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Cartoons are evaluated on relevance to theme, creativity and originality, artistic composition and design, technique and use of medium, and overall visual impact."},{"Title":"Rangoli","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.15 (Fine Arts - Rangoli)","Sections":{"About":["Participants create a Rangoli design on a subject, theme or topic announced at the start of the event.","Participants may draw from traditional forms such as Mandna, Alpana, Alekhan, Kolam, Rangoli or others. Interpretations are allowed in freehand, pictorial or descriptive styles."],"TimeAndFormat":["Participants get a total of 2 hours and 30 minutes to finish the artwork. The events at a glance table prints a minimum of 120 minutes and a maximum of 150 minutes."],"Rules":["One participant.","Each Rangoli design is at most 4 feet x 4 feet (4 feet diameter for a circular rangoli). It must not be smaller than 2.5 feet x 2.5 feet (2.5 feet diameter for a circular rangoli).","The Rangoli must be made within and on the space given by the organizers.","Participants bring their own materials.","All work must be done freehand."],"Allowed":["Rangoli powders or colours, flower petals, coloured sawdust, or food grains (for example rice and lentils) are acceptable materials."],"NotAllowed":["Pasting or gluing of materials is strictly prohibited.","Dies, stencils, moulds, mechanical tools and any other aids are not permitted.","The use or possession of mobile phones and other digital devices is strictly prohibited for participants throughout the event."],"Judging":["Rangolis are evaluated on relevance to the theme, creativity and innovation, design and composition, neatness and precision, and colour harmony and aesthetic appeal."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Participants create a Rangoli design on a subject, theme or topic announced at the start of the event.\\n- Participants may draw from traditional forms such as Mandna, Alpana, Alekhan, Kolam, Rangoli or others. Interpretations are allowed in freehand, pictorial or descriptive styles.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Participants get a total of 2 hours and 30 minutes to finish the artwork. The events at a glance table prints a minimum of 120 minutes and a maximum of 150 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One participant.\\n- Each Rangoli design is at most 4 feet x 4 feet (4 feet diameter for a circular rangoli). It must not be smaller than 2.5 feet x 2.5 feet (2.5 feet diameter for a circular rangoli).\\n- The Rangoli must be made within and on the space given by the organizers.\\n- Participants bring their own materials.\\n- All work must be done freehand.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Rangoli powders or colours, flower petals, coloured sawdust, or food grains (for example rice and lentils) are acceptable materials.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Pasting or gluing of materials is strictly prohibited.\\n- Dies, stencils, moulds, mechanical tools and any other aids are not permitted.\\n- The use or possession of mobile phones and other digital devices is strictly prohibited for participants throughout the event.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Rangolis are evaluated on relevance to the theme, creativity and innovation, design and composition, neatness and precision, and colour harmony and aesthetic appeal."},{"Title":"Cultural Procession","Source":"Rules and Regulations p.16-17 (Cultural Procession)","Sections":{"About":["Contingents may represent the culture of any State or Region, or National Integrity or Culture as a whole. All universities are encouraged to take part in the Cultural Procession with the same spirit as the other competitive events.","There are two types of participation. Introductory Participation: a university that does not perform any activity in the procession. Before the last performance (of the host team or university), all universities under Introductory Participation march together, and the Presenter or Anchor announces the names of the universities and their Vice Chancellors. The organizing university collects this information in advance.","Performance Participation (demonstration or performance of cultural troops): the Presenter or Anchor announces the name of the performing university as it enters the procession, with a positive note and the name of its Vice Chancellor."],"TimeAndFormat":["The Cultural Procession is held on the inaugural day, before the formal inaugural ceremony.","The procession starts with the Flag Off ceremony.","The route can be 1 to 2 km long or more, depending on the space at the host university.","A stage or performance area is provided at one point, towards the end, for teams to show their cultural performance for 3 to 5 minutes at the Zonal Youth Festivals and 2 to 3 minutes at the National Youth Festival.","The previous year's overall champion of the zonal festival leads the procession and the host university is last. The other teams follow in alphabetical order."],"Rules":["Team Managers or Contingent In-charges must deposit two flags of their university at the desk near the registration desk. The flags are hoisted on poles before the procession begins. The ideal flag size is 6 feet x 4 feet.","The host university provides flag poles to all contingents for carrying and showing flags during the procession.","Teams are advised to bring local or regional costumes that show their culture.","A university may bring a university banner, to be carried by the contingent during the procession. A banner is not mandatory. The preferred size is 10 feet x 3 feet.","The host university provides a PA system with three microphones and the means to play different recorded music or audio."],"Allowed":["Recorded music is allowed for Cultural Procession performances."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judgment of performances begins from the start of the procession and continues until it is officially declared finished."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Contingents may represent the culture of any State or Region, or National Integrity or Culture as a whole. All universities are encouraged to take part in the Cultural Procession with the same spirit as the other competitive events.\\n- There are two types of participation. Introductory Participation: a university that does not perform any activity in the procession. Before the last performance (of the host team or university), all universities under Introductory Participation march together, and the Presenter or Anchor announces the names of the universities and their Vice Chancellors. The organizing university collects this information in advance.\\n- Performance Participation (demonstration or performance of cultural troops): the Presenter or Anchor announces the name of the performing university as it enters the procession, with a positive note and the name of its Vice Chancellor.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The Cultural Procession is held on the inaugural day, before the formal inaugural ceremony.\\n- The procession starts with the Flag Off ceremony.\\n- The route can be 1 to 2 km long or more, depending on the space at the host university.\\n- A stage or performance area is provided at one point, towards the end, for teams to show their cultural performance for 3 to 5 minutes at the Zonal Youth Festivals and 2 to 3 minutes at the National Youth Festival.\\n- The previous year's overall champion of the zonal festival leads the procession and the host university is last. The other teams follow in alphabetical order.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Team Managers or Contingent In-charges must deposit two flags of their university at the desk near the registration desk. The flags are hoisted on poles before the procession begins. The ideal flag size is 6 feet x 4 feet.\\n- The host university provides flag poles to all contingents for carrying and showing flags during the procession.\\n- Teams are advised to bring local or regional costumes that show their culture.\\n- A university may bring a university banner, to be carried by the contingent during the procession. A banner is not mandatory. The preferred size is 10 feet x 3 feet.\\n- The host university provides a PA system with three microphones and the means to play different recorded music or audio.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Recorded music is allowed for Cultural Procession performances.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judgment of performances begins from the start of the procession and continues until it is officially declared finished."}]`),o=[],r=[{Key:"AgeLimitDate",Kind:"text",Label:"Date on which the age limit is checked",Value:"1 July of the current academic year",Source:"Rules and Regulations p.18 (Eligibility Rules)"},{Key:"RegistrationFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Registration fee",Value:"INR 3500 per participant, including each team official",Source:"Rules and Regulations p.19 (Registration/Participation Fee)"},{Key:"CautionMoney",Kind:"fee",Label:"Caution money (refundable)",Value:"INR 5000 (Rupees five thousand only) per participating university",Source:"Rules and Regulations p.20 (Caution Money)"},{Key:"ProtestFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Protest fee",Value:"INR 1000 (One thousand) only",Source:"Rules and Regulations p.21 (Judgment and Appeals)"},{Key:"QueriesContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"Contact for queries",Value:{Name:"AIU Youth Affairs",Role:"Queries about the festival",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:"youthaffairs.aiu@gmail.com"},Source:"Rules and Regulations p.21 (Contact Us)"}],l=[{Claim:"Every eligibility, contingent, fee, discipline, safety, judging, protest and per-event rule on the page is from the AIU Rules and Regulations for the 39th Inter-University Youth Festival (UNIFESTs) 2025-26. Page 1 of the PDF is the Events at a Glance table.",SourceType:"Primary - Association of Indian Universities (AIU) rules and regulations",Source:"AIU 39th Inter-University Youth Festival (UNIFESTs) 2025-26 Rules and Regulations (21 pages)",Url:"https://mdsuajmer.ac.in/notifications/2190_Rules%20and%20Guidelines%20by%20AIU%20for%20youth%20fest.pdf"},{Claim:"Participant, accompanist and time limits per event, the grace times (15 and 30 seconds) and the placing points (group 9-7-5, solo 5-3-1) are from the Events at a Glance table.",SourceType:"Primary - Association of Indian Universities (AIU) events at a glance",Source:"AIU 39th Inter-University Youth Festival 2025-26 Events at a Glance (1 page)",Url:"https://aiu.ac.in/wp-content/uploads/docs/2025/12/Final_Events_at_a_Glance.pdf"}],u={TemplateKey:e,Year:2026,Note:t,Page:n,ParticipantTypes:a,AgeGroups:i,Competitions:s,CompetitionAgeGroups:o,Variables:r,Evidence:l};export{i as AgeGroups,o as CompetitionAgeGroups,s as Competitions,l as Evidence,t as Note,n as Page,a as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,r as Variables,d as Year,u as default};
